<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nchare Yen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 14th century</span> · Also known as Nchare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nchare Yen was, according to Bamum tradition, a Tikar prince who conquered the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foumban">Foumban</a> in the western grassfields of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> and became the first mfon (king) of Bamum, traditionally in 1394. The dynasty he founded ruled continuously, and the later king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-njoya">Ibrahim Njoya</a> recorded his story in the history written in the Bamum script.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nchare-yen.jpg" alt="Nchare Yen" width="152" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khu'hamgaba Kitap · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nchare_Yen_picture.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
